GitHub code search found the submitDappRequest() call only in pi-dapp-service.html, not a function implementation. Thus, on a deployment that serves exactly the inspected branch, the submission and request-history features are likely broken. This is not a claim that the live site was browser-tested.
3. Supabase read-only findings
Projects checked:
Mainnet: ribpntyqdleytsyktdfb
Testnet: vhvkwvngmrlgyzwemttt
Read-only catalog queries searched public and albukhr_security for matching table names and function names containing terms such as dapp, service, launch, quote, agreement, deliverable, milestone, and receipt.
Mainnet: no matching service-specific tables or RPC/function names found.
Testnet: no matching service-specific tables or RPC/function names found.
Storage: no dedicated dApp-service or receipt bucket found. The Mainnet query returned external-project-documents, a private External Projects bucket; do not reuse it for dApp receipts without a separate security and access-policy design. No matching bucket was found in Testnet.
No SQL writes or migrations were run.
4. Admin workflow
Searches of MuhmdBuharisaeed/albukhr-admin for “Pi dApp service”, “dapp request”, and receiptRef returned no matching dedicated admin implementation. An admin review queue, receipt verification workflow, status transitions, and customer messaging therefore remain unverified/not present in the inspected admin code search.
A new Admin workflow should follow existing ALBUKHR admin authentication/MFA and server-side authorization patterns. It should not create a parallel authentication system or reuse External Projects permissions by default.
